control: The chart ships the tested alerting rules where the Prometheus Operator's API is served
removes: the template renders the rules whether or not the operator's API is served
packages: ./ratelimit/lease
tests: TestTheChartShipsTheRulesWhereTheOperatorsAPIIsServed
scheduled-count: no

diff --git a/packaging/chart/templates/prometheusrule.yaml b/packaging/chart/templates/prometheusrule.yaml
index f5e7a58b..be14d214 100644
--- a/packaging/chart/templates/prometheusrule.yaml
+++ b/packaging/chart/templates/prometheusrule.yaml
@@ -2,11 +2,11 @@
 The alerting rules of ADR-0077 as the Prometheus Operator's resource. It renders where the cluster serves the
 PrometheusRule kind, or when monitoring.prometheusRule.enabled forces it on, and never when it is false, so the chart
 assumes only core Kubernetes (ADR-0052). A platform without the operator loads rules/alerting-rules.yaml its own
 way. The rules are that file embedded whole, which is the file promtool tests.
 */ -}}
-{{- if include "mm.monitoringEnabled" (list $ .Values.monitoring.prometheusRule.enabled "monitoring.coreos.com/v1/PrometheusRule") }}
+{{- if true }}
 apiVersion: monitoring.coreos.com/v1
 kind: PrometheusRule
 metadata:
   name: {{ include "mm.fullname" . }}-alerting-rules
   namespace: {{ .Release.Namespace }}
